it_big_tech_vocab_001 the Technological solutionism => le solutionnisme technologique | alts: ['le technosolutionnisme']
R Critical academic and media term for treating technical fixes as sufficient answers to complex political or social problems.
T Solutionnisme is not neutral problem-solving: it criticizes the reduction of political choices and structural conflicts to technical problems.
X Le solutionnisme technologique promet une application pour chaque crise sociale, mais élude les rapports de pouvoir et les responsabilités institutionnelles qui la structurent.
E Technological solutionism promises an app for every social crisis, but evades the power relations and institutional responsibilities that structure it.
C ['Le solutionnisme technologique']
