N Old_back is lexically sound after lowercasing the common-noun metaphor. Self-review replaced a generic rivalry example with concrete mechanisms spanning trade, industry and standards.
it_big_tech_vocab_063 the Digital Belt and Road => les Routes de la soie numériques | alts: []
R Established geopolitical and infrastructure-policy name for the digital component of China’s Belt and Road Initiative; French institutional usage often favors the plural.
T The literal Ceinture et Route numériques is not the conventional French name; French policy writing uses Route or Routes de la soie numériques.
X Les Routes de la soie numériques associent câbles, centres de données et promotion de normes chinoises, tout en renforçant l’influence de Pékin.
E The Digital Silk Roads combine cables, data centers, and the promotion of Chinese standards while strengthening Beijing’s influence.
C ['Les Routes de la soie numériques']
N Materially replaces old_back’s literal Ceinture et Route numériques with the established French name. Self-review removed a number-changing alternative that was not directly substitutable in the example and repaired an overextended use of déployer.
it_big_tech_vocab_064 Techno-nationalism => le techno-nationalisme | alts: ['le technonationalisme']
R Established innovation-policy and geopolitical term for linking national power, security and autonomy to domestic technological capacity.
T It is broader than nationalisme des données because it also covers industrial capacity, research, standards, procurement and supply chains.
X Le techno-nationalisme lie la maîtrise des semi-conducteurs à la sécurité nationale et justifie des subventions, des contrôles d’exportation ainsi qu’une préférence pour les fournisseurs nationaux.
