it_big_tech_vocab_054 the Post-capitalist digital economy | Transparent compositional phrase rather than a stable specialist headword; the prompt identifies no particular post-capitalist model.
it_big_tech_vocab_056 the Digital accumulation | Unstable, underspecified collocation that does not identify whether capital, data, power, reputation or another resource is being accumulated.
it_big_tech_vocab_057 Techno-regulation | Ambiguous without context between regulation of technology and regulation implemented through technology, so no single production-ready French headword is defensible.
it_big_tech_vocab_060 the Algorithmic class struggle | Unstable rhetorical composition rather than a fixed concept; the retained algorithmic-exploitation card teaches the concrete labor relation without reifying the slogan.
it_big_tech_vocab_062 Technological sovereignty | Near-duplicates the already-authored b01 Digital sovereignty card, whose register note already records technological sovereignty as the related broader variant.
it_big_tech_vocab_067 the Data-driven modes of production | Transparent paraphrase adding no stable concept beyond the retained digital mode of production and data-centered examples elsewhere in the chunk.
it_big_tech_vocab_069 the Silicon Road | Weakly lexicalized and ambiguous among a trade route, semiconductor supply chain or branded geopolitical initiative.
it_big_tech_vocab_070 the Technological mode of power | Malformed or nonstandard theoretical phrase with no stable meaning or context fixing what mode of power is intended to denote.
it_big_tech_vocab_072 Digital authoritarianism | Conceptually duplicates the already-authored b01 Techno-authoritarianism card without supplying a distinct analytical tradition or scope.
it_big_tech_vocab_074 the Information economy | Économie de l’information is a transparent, familiar policy term for a C1 learner, and the bare prompt supplies no narrower analytical sense.
it_big_tech_vocab_075 Digital dialectics | Vague theoretical collocation without an author or proposition identifying the intended contradiction or even a fixed singular or plural term.
it_big_tech_vocab_076 Techno-globalization | Rare, underspecified coinage with no stable analytical content beyond the transparent interaction of technology and globalization.
it_big_tech_vocab_077 the Post-industrial class struggle | Compositional slogan rather than an established headword; the prompt identifies neither the post-industrial class formation nor the conflict intended.
it_big_tech_vocab_078 Digital solidarity | Transparent and semantically broad value phrase whose meaning depends on context and offers no distinctive French production lesson.

