E Cloud imperialism takes hold when public administrations depend on foreign infrastructure whose contractual terms, keys, and avenues for redress they do not control.
C ['L’impérialisme du cloud']
N Old_back is defensible after lowercasing the article. Confidence is moderate because the label remains emerging; self-review stated its evaluative register explicitly and replaced an unnatural claim about mastering a jurisdiction.
it_big_tech_vocab_087 the Gig economy => l’économie à la tâche | alts: ['l’économie des petits boulots']
R Economy and labor-policy term for income organized as successive short assignments; the alternative is common and more journalistic or socially evaluative.
T The legacy économie gigogne is nonsensical: gig means a short paid job here, whereas gigogne describes objects nested inside one another.
X L’économie à la tâche promet de la flexibilité aux livreurs, mais fait peser sur eux les temps d’attente non rémunérés, l’entretien du véhicule et le risque économique.
